아래 함수 좀 정리해줄 수 있어? 결과는 지금이랑 똑같이 나와야 하고, if가 너무 깊게 들어가 있어서 읽기가 힘들어.

def calc_fee(user, amount):
    if user is not None:
        if user.grade == 'VIP':
            if amount > 100000:
                return amount * 0.01
            else:
                return amount * 0.015
        else:
            if amount > 100000:
                return amount * 0.02
            else:
                return amount * 0.03
    else:
        return None

Every time I run plan it wants to destroy and recreate this bucket even though I only touched the tags. Any idea what's forcing the replacement?

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "reports" {
  bucket = "${var.env}-${random_id.suffix.hex}-reports"
  tags = {
    Team = "finance-data"
    Env  = var.env
  }
}

resource "random_id" "suffix" {
  byte_length = 4
  keepers = {
    tags = jsonencode(var.common_tags)
  }
}

A contractor wrote this endpoint for our internal image tool. Something about it makes me uneasy — could someone outside abuse the file parameter?

app.get('/thumb', (req, res) => {
  const name = req.query.file;
  exec(`convert uploads/${name} -resize 200x200 /tmp/thumb_${name}`, (err) => {
    if (err) return res.status(500).send('failed');
    res.sendFile(`/tmp/thumb_${name}`);
  });
});

이 PR 머지해도 될지 봐줘. 이체 한도 체크하는 부분인데 뭔가 찜찜해서.

func (s *TransferService) Check(ctx context.Context, acc *Account, amt int64) error {
	limit, _ := s.repo.DailyLimit(ctx, acc.ID)
	used, _ := s.repo.UsedToday(ctx, acc.ID)
	if used+amt > limit {
		return ErrLimitExceeded
	}
	go s.repo.AddUsage(ctx, acc.ID, amt)
	return nil
}

